review['title']={'review_scope':'ACTUAL_TITLE','source_refs':refs,'analysis':'At What Age Most People Hit $100K, $500K & $1M (Not What You Think) combines measurable wealth thresholds with age comparison and a surprise promise. It addresses anxiety about falling behind and supplies a progression rather than one static target. The script explicitly answers each threshold, so topical alignment is strong; evidence alignment is weak. Most People implies a representative attainment distribution, while the29 figure traces to selected forum respondents,49 to sampled millionaires and the500K age is unverified. A responsible reuse would name the population and distinguish wealth stocks from milestone histories.','search_demand':'Plausible net-worth-by-age and first100K curiosity;historical query volume unavailable.','script_alignment':'Direct numeric answer,unsupported general-population framing and selected-sample drift.','peer_comparison_ids':comparison}
review['thumbnail']={'review_scope':'ACTUAL_IMAGE','source_refs':refs,'analysis':'Registered authentic1280×720 image has a white field,large black $100K→$1M across the top,a cartoon man on the left holding a green cash-filled jar on a small table,a green stopwatch centrally,and a curved black arrow pointing to stacked green bills at lower right. The numeric progression,arrow and stopwatch remain clear at320×180;jar details become small but major shapes remain readable. The title asks when;the image promises movement from one wealth tier to another. Green money and the stopwatch make accumulation/time concrete. The cash imagery can blur liquid savings with net worth including home equity,which matters to the factual promise. No exact age is printed. Current authentic retrieval does not establish upload-era design,CTR or causal performance.','image_path':f'research/finance-economics-intelligence/audit-batches/NICK_{V}.jpg','image_source':f'https://i.ytimg.com/vi/{V}/maxresdefault.jpg','image_sha256':sha(O/'registered-thumbnail.jpg'),'dimensions':[1280,720],'mobile_review_width':320,'historical_design':'UNKNOWN','performance_effect':'UNKNOWN;NO_PRIVATE_ANALYTICS'}
review['script']={'review_scope':'FULL_STORED_TEXT','source_refs':refs,'source':old['script']['source'],'stored_text_completeness':f'All {len(S)} canonical characters read in three contiguous witnessed ranges;auto-generated untimed text;audio, timed delivery and editing unverified. Complete stored opening/ending reviewed;completeness against actual narration unknown.','audio_verified':False,'timing':'OPENING_WORDS_ONLY','opening_words':first,'ending_words':last,'analysis':'The hook invokes social comparison,sleepless retirement worries and repeated app-checking before promising exact milestone ages. Nick introduces credibility and a subscribe request,then rejects a linear lifecycle. The body climbs100K→250K→500K→1M→2M,using effort-versus-compounding metaphors and one-year8%examples. A second pass repeats the milestones and psychological freedom before adding generational inequality,rent and downpayment barriers. The closing compresses mixed evidence into a universal age schedule and returns to the app-checking joke. Repetition can clarify the ladder but also amplifies unsupported ages. The initial community-survey caveat is useful and then lost. The midpoint changes wealth-rank evidence into income rank,while net worth silently becomes an invested portfolio or passive income. Dollar growth is mathematically conditional;retirement sustainability is unmodeled. Exact claim quotes and offsets in40groups distinguish source limitations from arithmetic errors. This is text structure,not observed editing,acting,music,motion or retention.','beat_map':['Social-media comparison,3am retirement anxiety and checking apps establish personal stakes;promise exact ages.','Reject a universal linear path;ordinary-millionaire story and comparison rationale.','First100K:community survey29/95th39,selection caveat,then unsupportedmid30s correction.','250K and500K escalation;8%illustrations shift from effort to growth;17%eventual claim lacks source.','Millionaire49,countgrowth and household-percentage claims;2M extension.','Second tour repeats milestones,tenfold dollar potential and work-freedom psychology.','Generational wealth split changes wealth percentile into earners;housing/rent/downpayments add structural barriers.','Personal25/50K and35/200K benchmarks;inheritance/debt and repeated cohort account.','Closing age schedule drops earlier denominator caveat;consistent investing/lifestyle restraint/app-checking callback.'],'claim_audit':[{k:v for k,v in c.items() if k not in ['original_quote','missing_assumptions','wealth_definition','population_and_age','calculation_receipts']} for c in claims]}
review['topic']={'review_scope':'FULL_TRANSCRIPT_TOPIC','source_refs':refs,'analysis':'Personal wealth benchmarking by age with a compounding ladder and generational-housing context. The audience problem is uncertainty about progress rather than selecting a financial product. Valid educational mechanisms are reinvested returns,contributions,liabilities and housing costs. The title demands first-attainment evidence that neither cross-sectionalSCFmedians nor community respondents can supply for all Americans. Total net worth includes illiquid equity and is distinct from savings,retirement-account assets or an8%-earning portfolio. Explicitly separate observed age-band wealth,threshold prevalence,retrospective first crossings and prospective personal scenarios. NoSCFmedian was converted to a replacement exact age.','audience_problem':'Assess progress without mistaking selected success stories or broad household age bins for an individual deadline.','economic_mechanism':'COMPOUNDING_CONTRIBUTIONS_NET_WORTH_DEFINITIONS_SELECTION_AND_COHORT_EFFECTS','demand_type':'EVERGREEN_WEALTH_MILESTONE_AND_SOCIAL_COMPARISON','time_sensitivity':'High for wealth distributions,nominal thresholds,housing and survey vintages;lower for conditional compound-growth arithmetic.','narrative_angle':'Milestone ladder moves from hard first savings to autonomous growth,then generational barriers temper the optimism.','novelty_and_corpus_angle':'An original treatment could show four separate panels:age-band net worth distribution,share above a threshold,selected retrospective milestone histories,and adjustable personal scenarios. Add homeequity-versus-investable assets and a variable-return downturn. No universal age schedule or promised millionaire outcome.','competition':context}
review['virality']={'review_scope':'INDIVIDUAL_PUBLIC_EVIDENCE','source_refs':refs,'causal_status':'DESCRIPTIVE_ASSOCIATION_NOT_CAUSAL','analysis':f'Frozen115774views at286.5681days gives404.0017015views/day. Ten-peer median111.9088908,ratio{F["peer_ratio_10"]:.5f}STRONG;five-peer median128.4536125,ratio{F["peer_ratio_5"]:.5f}STRONG. Class stable across these windows. Numeric thresholds,age anxiety,surprise and cash/time imagery plausibly draw attention;public metadata cannot identify their causal contributions.','observed_result':'Frozen2026-09-11:115774views,2000likes,363comments;20:35longform. Snapshotdaytimezoneunknown;no refresh.','topic_demand':'Wealth milestone comparison plausibly relevant to existing personal-finance audience;actual search demand/traffic unavailable.','trend_timing':'Uploaded2025-11-28T10:22:00Z per archive;2023SCFreport,2016forum,2019Ramsey,2025UBSand2024housinganalysispre-dateupload.2026SCFreleaseandrebasingsareseparate,no retrospective leakage.','competition':context+';ten/five exact cohorts and frozen inputs in receipts.','format_fit':'Long form permits escalating milestones,repetition and generational context;actual visual pacing,delivery andretentionunverified.','channel_context':'Above nearest-age samechannel long-form lifetime-rate median in both cohorts;not a current growth rate or control for changing audience size.','alternative_explanations':['Unknown recommendation/impression distribution','UnknownCTR,retention,satisfaction and traffic sources','Prior channel audience and upload timing','Lifetime-rate and cohort-selection sensitivity','Unverified historical title/thumbnail changes'],'original_content_lesson':{'test':'Test an original benchmark ladder with transparent source populations and wealth definitions,then show contribution-dependent scenarios instead of universal age deadlines.','boundary':'Editorial hypothesis only;no causal packaging claim or performance guarantee.'}}
